# Continues the published route from walkthrough_03_kitchen.xit.
include walkthrough_03_kitchen.xit

# ============================================================
# Walkthrough, segment 4: the courier's package.
#
# Edsel said he would send the game "by courier as soon as I hang up", and
# the delivery is driven by the same event scheduler as the phone call: on
# the first WAIT after returning to the front hall the game reports "Time
# passes. You hear the doorbell sound." Every later WAIT is just "Time
# passes.", so the doorbell is a one-shot scheduled event, not a poll.
#
# The package is NOT handed over -- opening the door reveals an empty
# stoop ("You open the front door and immediately feel the force of the
# storm building outside.") and the parcel is sitting on it.
#
# Front hall hotspots, MEASURED by hover sweep:
#   door (270,42)   flowers (230,51)   switch (310,51)   table (230,80)
# and once the door is open, through the doorway:
#   front yard (280,40)   stoop (280,90)   package (280,100)
#
# The package region sits right at the bottom edge of the picture window,
# where the cursor sprite overlaps the label strip -- which is why the
# sweep that found it deliberately reads the label text rather than
# treating the strip as an opaque hash.
# ============================================================

# --- east, back to the lit front hall ---
move 37 148
run 5
click left
run 40
move 305 196
run 15
checkpoint wt4_hall_again

# --- WAIT once: the doorbell rings ---
key 0 59
run 30
checkpoint wt4_doorbell
shot build/frames/wt4_doorbell.bmp

# --- open the front door ---
move 14 37
run 5
click left
run 15
move 270 42
run 5
click left
run 70
move 305 196
run 15
checkpoint wt4_door_open
shot build/frames/wt4_door_open.bmp

# --- take the package off the stoop (2 points) ---
key 0 59
run 30
move 14 7
run 5
click left
run 15
move 280 100
run 5
click left
run 70
move 305 196
run 15
checkpoint wt4_package_taken
shot build/frames/wt4_package_taken.bmp
